# Verifying releases

[% if is_public %]
Release artifacts carry signed build provenance (Sigstore), produced in GitHub Actions.

```bash
gh attestation verify <file> --repo [[ github_owner ]]/[[ project_slug ]]
```
[% endif %]
[% if 'python' in languages %]

**PyPI:** packages are uploaded with trusted publishing and carry PEP 740 attestations, visible on the PyPI file page.
[% endif %]
[% if 'typescript' in languages %]

**npm:** packages are published with trusted publishing[% if is_public %] and npm provenance (`npm audit signatures` checks it)[% endif %].
[% endif %]
[% if 'rust' in languages %]

**crates.io:** crates are published with crates.io trusted publishing (short-lived token from GitHub OIDC).
[% endif %]

Each GitHub release also has an SBOM (SPDX JSON) attached.
